# Multi-Feature Architecture

The Finance Simulator is one SPA hosting multiple **features** (not separate apps).
Users switch features with a tab bar; there is no per-feature runtime isolation.
Background jobs keep running across tab switches.

## Naming

- **App**: "Finance Simulator"; app-wide prefix is **`fs`**.
- **Feature ids** (kebab-case): `withdraw` → "Withdraw"; `sor-lab` → "SOR Lab";
  `accumulate` → "Accumulate"; etc.
- Folders: `src/features/<feature-id>/` for feature-owned logic, UI, and partials.
- DOM: feature roots `id="feature-<feature-id>"`; new element ids prefixed
  `<feature-id>-...`.
- **Reserved:** bare `plan` / `FEATURE_PLAN` / `src/features/plan/` for a future
  household aggregator feature. Withdraw must not own those names.
- **`onTarget*`** in code/state means spending-target adherence scoring (UX may
  still say “on plan”); it is not the future Plan feature.

## Shared vs feature code

| Lives in | Examples |
|---|---|
| Shared (`src/core`, `src/ui`, `src/state`, `src/workers`, `src/partials/`, `src/data/`) | Scenario model + defaults/presets, RNG, sensitivity summarizer (`sensitivity.js`), workers + dispatcher handlers, chart theme/setup, dialogs, header, session chrome, feature registry, session/job abstractions, historical returns (`data/historicalData.js`), history sampling (`core/history.js`), allocation glide math (`core/allocation.js`) |
| Feature (`src/features/<id>/`) | Feature partials, input wiring, results/report UI, feature charts, run orchestration, Lab variable registry, Withdraw history UI wrapper (`withdraw/history.js`) |

Truly shared code stays shared. Risk-preset *data* (`src/state/presets/`) stays
shared with the scenario model; only the Easy Mode UI lives under the feature.
Feature-specific code must not reach into another feature's DOM or module state —
consume scenarios only through `scenario.js` / session-store interfaces.

SOR Lab keeps sweep *results* in memory (config + Withdraw dependency snapshots are
what save/share). Visualizations read stored curves through pure selectors — do
not bake tornado-only shapes into the persisted result model.

### Shared assets (no feature forks)

Return tables and allocation math are **shared-only**. Features must not copy or
fork `src/data/historicalData.js`, `src/core/history.js`, or
`src/core/allocation.js`. Cross-feature investable-class contract:

- **`ALLOCATION_ENGINE_KEYS`** (`src/core/allocation.js`) — camelCase six classes
  (`usLgGrowth` … `cash`), no inflation.
- **`LOGNORMAL_ORDER`** (`src/core/history.js`) — snake_case history keys including
  `inflation`.
- **Returns / allocation UI** is shared via
  [`src/state/returnsAllocationSlice.js`](../../src/state/returnsAllocationSlice.js)
  (pure slice + `distMethod` canonicalize) and
  [`src/ui/returnsAllocation/controller.js`](../../src/ui/returnsAllocation/controller.js)
  (mountable year range / distribution / allocation panel). Withdraw keeps legacy
  DOM ids through a thin wrapper in `src/features/withdraw/history.js`;
  Accumulate and Social Security mount the shared controller. Do not fork
  per-feature history/allocation panels.

### Worker dispatcher

One worker bundle ([`src/workers/simulation.worker.js`](../../src/workers/simulation.worker.js))
routes by message `type` via [`dispatch.js`](../../src/workers/dispatch.js) to
handlers under `src/workers/handlers/`. Domain math stays in `src/core/`;
handlers must not import `src/features/*`. Later features add a handler module +
a `HANDLERS` map entry that calls their `src/core/<domain>.js`. Unknown types
post `{ type: 'error', … }` and do not open a pool.

Withdraw worker message types: `withdraw`, `withdrawGoalSeek`.

## Storage namespaces

- localStorage:
  - `fs:app:<key>` — genuinely cross-feature prefs only (theme, active tab).
  - `fs:<feature-id>:<key>` — feature state (autosave, report band, accordions,
    chart view prefs). **When in doubt, use the feature namespace.**
- IndexedDB: single `fs-sessions` database, `sessions` store, records keyed by
  `[feature, name]` (Phase 2+).
- Export envelope: `type: "fs-scenario"` plus `feature` and per-feature
  `stateVersion`; dependency snapshots carry their own `feature` +
  `stateVersion` + `state`. Optional top-level **`cashflowSeries`** (see below)
  may ride along on export/share.
- **Clean break**: ignore legacy `sor:*` / `sor-plan` localStorage keys, the old
  `sor-sessions` IndexedDB database, and legacy `sor-scenario` file imports.
  Legacy share-link URL params are ignored (open fresh, no decode, no error).
  Do not dual-read envelope `schemaVersion` on `fs-scenario` payloads.

### Cashflow series (producers only today)

- Versioned contract in [`src/state/cashflowSeries.js`](../../src/state/cashflowSeries.js):
  signed real-$ annual amounts by strategy, plus metadata (`sourceFeature`,
  `sessionName`, `startAge`, `units: 'real-dollars'`).
- Producers: Accumulate, Social Security, Roth Convert, House Equity attach
  via session-adapter **`getCashflowSeries`** on export/share. Import accepts
  and preserves the field but **does not** feed it into Withdraw math or UI.
- **Reserved for a future Plan feature:** Plan (or a household orchestrator)
  consuming imported series, and hard-linking one saved session per feature.
  Do not half-build that consumer inside Withdraw.

### State versioning & migrations

- Every session record, export/share envelope, and dependency snapshot writes
  **`stateVersion`** for that feature (Withdraw uses `SCHEMA_VERSION`; Lab uses
  `LAB_STATE_VERSION`).
- All migrate implementations and the dispatch registry live in
  [`src/state/migrations.js`](../../src/state/migrations.js)
  (`migrateScenario`, `migrateLabState`, `registerFeatureMigrator`,
  `migrateFeatureState`). Persistence / sessions call the registry only —
  no per-feature `if` branches.
- Session adapters may declare `stateVersion` + `migrate`;
  `registerSessionAdapter` re-registers them into the same registry.
- Share links: full URL must be ≤ **8000** characters; over the limit, show
  “Share link is too large. Use Export instead.” and do not copy. Export is
  unrestricted.

## Feature registry

Register features via `src/state/features.js` (`registerFeature`,
`setActiveFeature`, `setFeatureBadge`, …). Tab bar under the title is rendered
from the registry. Active tab persists in `fs:app:prefs`.

### Placement (`primary` | `more`)

- `registerFeature({ …, placement })` — omit or `'primary'` for top-level tabs;
  `'more'` puts the feature under the More control (button + listbox).
- **Primary today:** `accumulate`, `withdraw` (tab order; default active is
  still `withdraw`). **More today:** `sor-lab`,
  `ss-timing`, `roth-convert`, `house-equity` (plus future features). More is always rendered, even if empty.
- When a More feature is active, the More control’s label becomes that feature’s
  title and the control is `aria-selected`. Escape closes the menu and returns
  focus to the More button.
- Busy/progress badges roll up onto the More control when any More feature has a
  running job; each menu item also shows its own badge.
- Narrow viewports keep equal-width cells for the primary tabs **plus More** —
  not one cell per every registered feature.

## Sessions & jobs (Phase 2+)

- Header session controls bind to the **active feature's** session store.
- Share/export payloads are feature-aware and self-contained: feature id + state +
  snapshot copies of cross-feature dependencies. On open/import, embed
  dependencies as named sessions with collision auto-rename — never overwrite
  the recipient's existing sessions.
- Jobs run through a shared job manager; they survive tab switches; results
  deliver to the owning feature; tabs show busy/progress badges.
- **Do not render Chart.js into a hidden feature root** (`display:none` sizes to
  zero). Defer render until `onActivate`, or call `chart.resize()` on activation.

## New-feature scaffold checklist

Reuse for each new feature (`accumulate`, `ss-timing`, `roth-convert`,
`house-equity`, …):

- `src/features/<id>/` with `index.js`, `session.js`, `run.js`, `partials/`, `ui/`
- `FEATURE_*` constant in [`src/state/storageKeys.js`](../../src/state/storageKeys.js)
- Register in [`src/main.js`](../../src/main.js); top-level feature partial
  (`src/features/<id>/partials/<id>.html` or equivalent) owns the
  `#feature-<id>` root and feature header copy; include it from
  `index.html`; partial dir added to `partialDirectory` in
  [`vite.config.js`](../../vite.config.js)
- Session adapter (`getState`, `applyState`, `stateVersion`, `migrate`,
  `getDependencies` / `getCashflowSeries` when applicable)
- Compute in `src/core/<domain>.js`, invoked via the worker dispatcher and
  [`jobs.js`](../../src/state/jobs.js)
- Charts rendered or resized in `onActivate` (hidden roots size to zero)
- Vitest for math; one thin Playwright smoke assertion
- Inline help copy + three named presets
